I made a couple errors.  First:

>Grayswandir is an interesting case.  It behaves as Frost Brand in
>doubling damage, but since it is a saber and not a longsword, it does
>only (1d8)*2 against both small and large.  Since it is silver, it
>does an extra 1d20 damage against silver-hating monsters such as
>shades.  This damage is not doubled.

Yes it is.  The damage is doubled and affects vampires, demons,
were-creatures, and shades.  That means that a blessed +6
Grayswandir does 2*(1d8+1d20+1d4+6) damage to these creatures, for an
average of 47 points of damage!  This is clearly the best weapon to
use against one of these critters.

Vorpal Blade is +1 to damage so:

Normal:
Vorpal Blade	  5.5 *		   9.5 *

Enchanted +6 weapon:
Vorpal Blade	 11.5 *		  15.5 *

